    "created_at": "2023-05-26T23:17:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-26T23:17:49Z",
    "body": "I agree with the comments above that we shouldn't mix the **invoker** and the **anchor**. It's possible that we could decide to make the invoking element an \"implicit anchor element\" but there's a separate question about whether we need to *expose* that implicit anchor element as a Javascript property.\r\n\r\nNote that in all of your imperative examples in the OP, you can use `popover.anchorElement = invokingElement` and things should work. In the declarative examples, since they're declarative, the \"right\" way to do this is just to add `<div popover anchor=anchor-id>`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
